===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Freon}}

===Etymology===
Genericization of the Chemours trademark "[[Freon]]." According to Flood, the name was formed from {{m|en|freeze}} and the arbitrary suffix {{m|en|-on}}.<ref>Flood, W.E., The Origins of Chemical Names, London: Oldbourne Book Co., 1963.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-freon.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|organic compound}} Any of several non-flammable [[refrigerant]]s based on [[halogenate]]d [[hydrocarbon]] including [[R-12]], [[R-22]], and [[R-23]].
# {{lb|en|refrigeration|slang}} A gaseous ozone-depleting [[refrigerant]]
# {{lb|en|environmentalism|slang}} A [[chlorofluorocarbon]]

